  "details": "This has been a long time standing issue for me. When I go to load an avatar and it takes a while (maybe due to a lack of optimization) and I have my menu open (due to just selecting the avatar) my menu flies a maximum distance away from me and is still interactable from this distance. Usually the menu flies into the ground. I'm not sure if this is intentional but a better behavior would be freezing the menu and its distance from the player in place while the avatar loads and then allowing it to move freely again when the avatar is done loading. \n\nThis appears to only affect me on PCVR and not on desktop mode. \n\nI have not attempted to replicate this issue on Quest.",
